test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-23T00:04:44.7948584Z             "body": "This draft adds the local batch/job engine and hardens durable journal initialization, evidence retention, cancellation witnesses, and browser diagnostics. The latest runtime implementation is ab4e111; b2cbc63 adds its terminal evidence and acceptance report only.\n\nNative99 completed: batch 1,665 passed / 5 failed; original 605 / 3; total 2,270 / 8 with no reported skips/cancellations. The primary Mac actual-client timeout at922 is separate from these counts. Linux/Windows actual Codex1000 and the separate Mac diagnostic pass. All five installed-package checks,617 component tests,12 schema races,32 recovery/publication boundaries and60 cancellation observations pass.\n\nRelease remains blocked by four first-JPEG/metadata failures, Windows zero-contact browser startup exhausting its fixed budget, Windows WebKit media readiness, and the primary Mac actual-client timeout. Earlier unconfirmed Windows process identities/exits remain unresolved; healthy later samples never clear them. The explicit-viewport experiment was rejected. No limits/assertions were weakened, no frame skip/warmup/encoder workaround applied, and prepared core stays9f9750ae.\n\nLocal final component suites154/154 on Node22 and24; package smokes, typecheck, workflow validation and archive/link verification pass. Node20 durable jobs remain unsupported. All18 native logs and the ordinary retry after an initial empty invalid-zip retrieval are archived. Earlier local namespace raw-log loss is explicitly disclosed.\n\nEvidence: [report](docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md), [blockers](docs/RELEASE_BLOCKERS.md), [native99 manifest](docs/evidence/native99-summary.json). Native runs: https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39868413381 and https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39868413347 . Subsequent docs-only CI must be assessed separately. Keep draft; no merge or release.\n",
